# ============================================================
# Bearings — HTTP headers (Netlify / Cloudflare Pages format)
# Strict CSP: connect-src 'self' enforces the no-external-data
# promise at the browser level. Any future external resource is a
# deliberate, visible edit here. See technical + privacy analysis.
#
# script-src and style-src are deliberately NOT set here. They are
# delegated to the per-page CSP <meta> emitted by Astro
# (security.csp in astro.config.mjs), which carries a sha256 hash
# for every inline script/style the build produces. If this header
# also declared script-src without those hashes, the two policies
# would intersect and every inline script would be blocked — the
# entire app (notes, sessions, theme, NightField) would be dead in
# production. scripts/check-csp.js verifies the built pages keep
# that contract. A page with no meta CSP is a build failure.
# ============================================================

/*
  Content-Security-Policy: connect-src 'self'; img-src 'self' data:; frame-src 'none'; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'; manifest-src 'self'
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Referrer-Policy: no-referrer
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(), camera=(), microphone=(), interest-cohort=()
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
